DESCRIPTION >
    Setup & Health: confirms a client-supplied verification token landed in the
    last 15 minutes. Tenant-scoped; prunes via (site_id, timestamp). Faithful
    1:1 port of setup-doctor.js's queryHogQL call at
    api/lib/setup-doctor.js:145 (queryName 'doctor_token_verify').
    Typed-column translation (SCOPE_v3.md §2.6): properties.site_id -> site_id.
    JSON-BAG FIELD HIT (flagged): properties.st_verify is in §2.6's JSON-bag
    list (alongside st_network/st_device/st_matchtype), not a typed column —
    read via JSONExtractString(properties, 'st_verify').
    Live query took the token VALUE as a second runtime input (the producer's
    sanitizeVerificationToken(verificationToken) output); ported as a second
    required template param (st_verify) rather than interpolated, matching
    HARD RULE #1's no-interpolation requirement for the tenant param and
    applying the same principle to this second user-supplied value.
    NOT YET PUSHED — validated read-only via `tb --cloud sql` only.

TOKEN "st_endpoint_read" READ

NODE doctor_token_verify_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT count() AS token_verify_count
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND JSONExtractString(properties, 'st_verify') = {{ String(st_verify, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp >= now() - INTERVAL 15 MINUTE

TYPE endpoint
